A nourishing, comforting vegetable soup packed with green cabbage, celery, bell peppers, and scallions in a rich tomato-vegetable broth seasoned with dry onion soup mix.

*Adapted from [The Spruce Eats](https://www.thespruceeats.com/one-week-cabbage-soup-diet-3061110).*

## Ingredients

- 1 can (48 oz) tomato-based vegetable juice (such as V8) or 6 cups water
- 1 to 2 cans (14.5 oz each) diced tomatoes
- ½ head green cabbage, chopped into bite-sized pieces
- 1 bunch celery, sliced
- 2 green bell peppers, seeded and chopped
- 6 large scallions (green onions), sliced
- 1 packet dry onion soup mix (such as Lipton)
- 1 to 2 bouillon cubes (vegetable, beef, or chicken; optional)
- Kosher salt and freshly ground black pepper, to taste
- Optional seasonings: ½ teaspoon curry powder, garlic powder, paprika, or chopped fresh parsley

## Instructions

1. **Load the Ingredients:** In a 6-quart stockpot, Dutch oven, or electric slow cooker, combine the chopped green cabbage, bell peppers, scallions, celery slices, and diced tomatoes along with their juices. Sprinkle in the dry onion soup mix and bouillon cubes (if using), then pour in the tomato-vegetable juice (or water). Stir everything together.
2. **Simmer Until Tender:**
   - **Stovetop Method:** Cover tightly with a lid and bring to an active boil over medium-high heat. Immediately reduce heat to low and let simmer gently for 1 hour, stirring every so often, until all vegetables become pleasantly tender.
   - **Slow Cooker Method:** Lock the lid in place and cook on LOW for 5 hours (or on HIGH for 3 hours).
3. **Infuse and Season:** Taste the broth and stir in salt, black pepper, and optional aromatic spices such as curry powder, garlic powder, or smoked paprika. Allow the soup to simmer for another 5 minutes on the stovetop (or 1 to 2 additional hours on Low in the slow cooker) to allow the herbs and spices to fully permeate the broth.
4. **Ladle and Serve:** Spoon steaming portions into deep soup bowls, finishing each serving with a sprinkle of freshly chopped parsley.

## Notes

- **Flavor Enhancements:** A pinch of red pepper flakes or a dash of hot sauce adds pleasant warmth.
- **Meal Prep:** This soup keeps exceptionally well in the refrigerator for up to 6 days and freezes well for up to 3 months.
